[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162706"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/assets/e1f3255f450e4761e20b64c0782a241a7d73637c9e276fa9c1e07227f26cf4e2.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above.\nWhat is the global minimum of the function?" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following definitions:\n\n- The global minimum of a function is the smallest value it attains on its domain. There can only be (at most) one global minimum.\n\n- A global minimum point is a point $(x,y,z)$ where a function reaches a global minimum. There can be zero, one, or many global minimum points.\n\nFor our function, the minimum value reached by the function is $f(x,y)=-3.$ Therefore, the global minimum is $-3.$ The function reaches this value at both $(x,y)=(1,-1)$ and $(x,y)=(1,2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/assets/1d257445551687ded71409efdce1b8695a9813a73ecb0fde5b6f4efccc6c15be.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163834/selection/eb556d9ccb061dff907af1e8a60f60128bbc5afddb249c8da76c193492c647dd" :answer/id #uuid "22ef0ad2-4522-5009-8152-65375ad59e28" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-2,1.2)$ and $(-2,1,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163834/selection/a28ef53f5b37d9b33acfa7dc83e72ce2442e7326e4b28f7bf66cdfd586addbaa" :answer/id #uuid "0384c97a-6ff5-5e21-92d7-1fcbb309bbda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,1,3)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163834/selection/631ae73e14a18b30ca42ff55cb14f3147b1905c7599fa797417e42102cbdd5e9" :answer/id #uuid "ff0ca9d9-f099-5bcb-8fd0-ff66651c7e42" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-2,1.2)$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163834/selection/8fa3f219dcc5e1c0c3c0d6772cec745fe7adee33954bf210c7e165a7c5a2a357" :answer/id #uuid "704fd941-9283-5860-b64d-2500fa8900a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,3,0)$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163834/selection/350e6e2cb1ae5ec1d1e0a336b980f52c15854277ceb4fec2c76855a99b3b9593" :answer/id #uuid "c05d199f-30b5-5416-874f-8a5b2a25f4b6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0,-2)$ and $(2,3,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163834/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4d01273-2d63-5d86-9542-66e1d59f44ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163834/selection/a28ef53f5b37d9b33acfa7dc83e72ce2442e7326e4b28f7bf66cdfd586addbaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-163834/selection/eb556d9ccb061dff907af1e8a60f60128bbc5afddb249c8da76c193492c647dd" "q-163834/selection/a28ef53f5b37d9b33acfa7dc83e72ce2442e7326e4b28f7bf66cdfd586addbaa" "q-163834/selection/631ae73e14a18b30ca42ff55cb14f3147b1905c7599fa797417e42102cbdd5e9" "q-163834/selection/8fa3f219dcc5e1c0c3c0d6772cec745fe7adee33954bf210c7e165a7c5a2a357" "q-163834/selection/350e6e2cb1ae5ec1d1e0a336b980f52c15854277ceb4fec2c76855a99b3b9593"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163834" :question/id #uuid "8c163c8c-12fc-59a2-9e1d-9f264f8ad03a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163834" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/assets/215b322e06280dd01e5858df9a17cd56673b5cdec69521decca205e03771ac21.png)\n\nThe graph $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above. What are the global maximum points of the function?" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following definitions:\n\n- The global maximum of a function is the largest value it attains on its domain. There can only be (at most) one global maximum.\n\n- A global maximum point is a point $(x,y,z)$ where a function reaches a global maximum. There can be zero, one, or many global maximum points.\n\nFor our function, the maximum value reached by the function is $f(x,y)=3.$ Therefore, the global maximum is $3.$ The function reaches this value when $(x,y)=(-2,1),$ so the global maximum point is $(-2,1,3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070363/assets/d5f948483a80f37257b285d48cd1e6bbf1d8a6ba9b66d1fea5edd865c787711a.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163834/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ee9cbe8-ad40-5155-b42d-1802f36adf27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163834"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164169/selection/6cc6e917bdd895d5be92d0e174b665d9b5f45687940e789f070cb305c98d254e" :answer/id #uuid "242c825a-e6e4-513b-a249-e790b380f43d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,3,0)$ and $(0,-2,-1.2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164169/selection/8f7f4f9f1561ef1b415bc14586276e6b656fce2a928f97354d57bd3b62b88ef9" :answer/id #uuid "19694ff0-6edb-5402-b06f-3a8588e09ca8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,1,-2)$ and $(0,-2,-1.2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164169/selection/364299c571b75c504250e020864c4355027484af05fe3d8a5d230462e82891f0" :answer/id #uuid "f8c76ce1-dd48-5357-9632-1f6dbec70853" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,1,-2)$ and $(-2,1,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164169/selection/1b5071d73b8dc6a1fa73582cf61f02a3a0115eb46456aa52eed30051a6fe2814" :answer/id #uuid "2ec04ce2-0c7d-5552-b6ea-9d1c06fb909c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,1,-2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164169/selection/8d7c1e7781ab547d9b762eb130fde9ca3425f61ed73afff551d0cc1be51061ec" :answer/id #uuid "c6ede4db-e774-5271-8fa4-c52322387059" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-2,-1.2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164169/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e63e6c34-4aee-5d2e-9936-1deab18ffbc6" :answer-field/key "